---
// Resources and actions in one plan: a GPU host whose playbook runs after it is created (illustrative,
// after turf-examples/use-cases/datacenter/ansible-k3s; `caller` is the triggering instance, as the
// engine evaluates it), an overlay trigger (verbatim from use-cases/datacenter/aicr-stack/aicr.turf.hcl),
// and the plan's "Actions to be invoked" lines, abridged.
---

<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2>Resources and actions, in one plan.</h2>
      <p>Desired state, and the steps between it: a playbook run once the hosts exist, a wait for a
        condition, a certification. Both are written in the Terraform language, both are planned, and
        both cross the approval point.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature">
      <div>
        <div class="codeblock">
          <div class="cb-head"><span>main.tf · a GPU host</span><span class="cb-legend">a playbook as a Terraform action</span></div>
<pre><span class="kw">resource</span> <span class="str">"aws_instance"</span> <span class="str">"gpu_host"</span> &#123;
  ami           = data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id
  instance_type = <span class="str">"g6.xlarge"</span>
  subnet_id     = aws_subnet.public.id
  key_name      = aws_key_pair.ops.key_name

  <span class="kw">lifecycle</span> &#123;
    <span class="kw">action_trigger</span> &#123;
      events     = [<span class="ev">after_create</span>]
      actions    = [action.ansible_playbook_run.host]
      on_failure = <span class="ev">taint</span>
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;

<span class="kw">action</span> <span class="str">"ansible_playbook_run"</span> <span class="str">"host"</span> &#123;
  <span class="kw">config</span> &#123;
    playbooks        = [<span class="str">"playbooks/gpu-host.yml"</span>]
    inventory_files  = [<span class="str">"$&#123;caller.public_ip&#125;,"</span>]
    user             = <span class="str">"ubuntu"</span>
    private_key_file = var.private_key_file
  &#125;
&#125;</pre>
          <div class="cb-note">illustrative · after turf-examples/use-cases/datacenter/ansible-k3s · <code>caller</code> is the instance that fired the trigger</div>
        </div>
        <div class="codeblock">
          <div class="cb-head"><span>aicr.turf.hcl · an overlay</span><span class="cb-legend">a trigger added without touching the module</span></div>
<pre><span class="kw">action_trigger</span> <span class="str">"certify"</span> &#123;
  target     = module.stack.module.gpu_operator.helm_release.this
  events     = [<span class="ev">after_create</span>]
  actions    = [action.turf_action.certify]
  on_failure = <span class="ev">taint</span>
&#125;</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3>Resource lifecycle hooks.</h3>
        <p>Terraform 1.16 actions, carried by Turf: a provider-defined operation hooked to one of six
          points in a resource’s lifecycle, planned beside the resource and applied inside the same run.
          OpenTofu has no action blocks.</p>
        <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="A plan excerpt: the GPU host will be created, and the host playbook action will be invoked after it.">
          <div class="term-head"><span>turf up · round 1</span></div>
          <div class="term-body">
<div class="t"><span class="dim"># aws_instance.gpu_host will be created</span></div>
<div class="t"><span class="ok">+ resource "aws_instance" "gpu_host"</span> <span class="dim">&#123; … &#125;</span></div>
<div class="t"> </div>
<div class="t"><span class="dim">  # Actions to be invoked after this change, in order:</span></div>
<div class="t"><span class="amber">  # action.ansible_playbook_run.host</span></div>
<div class="t"> </div>
<div class="t"><span class="b">Plan:</span> <span class="ok">1 to add.</span> <span class="b">Actions:</span> <span class="amber">1 to invoke.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="ticklist">
          <li><span class="g">✓</span><div><b>Before and after create, update, destroy</b> <span>— with
            <code>on_failure</code> set to halt, continue or taint, and a plan-time <code>condition</code>.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="g">✓</span><div><b>Overlays</b> <span>— a <code>*.turf.hcl</code> file adds a trigger with a
            <code>target</code> into any module, per environment or in memory for one run.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="g">✓</span><div><b>Ad-hoc runs</b> <span>— <code>invoke</code> runs a declared action now,
            with its own approval point and an audit record.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="g">✓</span><div><b>Day 2 is the same plan, again</b> <span>— a variable changes, the
            triggers re-fire at the right points, under the same approval.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
